      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Utwórz formularz bazując na następujących danych:\n\nChange of Employment Conditions Process Data\nThe data can be grouped into three main categories: data collected at the start, data retrieved for routing, and process status and description data.\n1. Application Data (The Initial Request)\nThis is the core data collected at the start of the process from the \"Change of Employment Conditions Application\".\n•\tEmployee Name (employee_name: String): The full name of the employee whose conditions are to be changed.\n•\tProposed Conditions (proposed_conditions: Text): The details of the change, such as the new proposed position, new salary, or other terms.\n•\tChange Justification (change_justification: Text): A text field explaining the reason for the change.\n•\tChange Effective Date (change_effective_date: Date): The date from which the new conditions should apply.\n2. Contextual and Routing Data (Internal System Data)\nThis is data that the process must look up from internal systems to make decisions and assign tasks.\n•\tIs an Academic Teacher? (is_academic_teacher: Boolean): It is used by the gateway \"Concerns an academic teacher?\" to route the request to either the Chancellor’s or the Rector’s approval path, as defined in the process. The variable should default to TRUE.\n3. Process Status and Decision Data (Generated During the Process)\nThis data is created as the request moves through the approval chain.\n•\tHead of O.U. Revie Status (head_of_ou_review_status: String): The outcome of the review by the Head of O.U. (e.g., ‘Approved’, ‘Rejected’, or other description).\n•\tPD Review Status (pd_review_status: String): The outcome of the review by the Personnel Department.\n•\tKWE Financial Opinion (kwe_financial_opinion: String): The financial opinion from the Quartermaster (e.g., ‘Funds_Available’, ‘No_Funds’).\n•\tPRK Opinion (prk_opinion: String): The opinion from the Vice-Rector for Education (if applicable).\n•\tPRN Opinion (prn_opinion: String): The opinion from the Vice-Rector for Scientific Affairs (if applicable).\n•\tFinal Decision (final_decision: String): The outcome (‘Approved’ or ‘Rejected’) set by either the Chancellor or the Rector.\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-04-03T10:35:37.060Z"
      },
